``` SR-05 | Dispatch Directory Bloat
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: The dispatch directory on the search head is filling the disk or
    holding thousands of artifacts; identify which users and saved searches
    are leaving the largest and longest-lived artifacts.
    Run on: SH-local for the artifact breakdown, SH for the warnings.
    Query: Warnings already raised (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/SR-05-probe.spl,
    probes/SR-05-probe-rest.spl to confirm the data it reads exists here.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=splunkd earliest=-7d (log_level=WARN OR log_level=ERROR)
    ("dispatch directory" OR "search artifacts" OR component=DispatchReaper)
| rex field=_raw "\]\s+-\s+(?<msg>.+)$"
| eval msg_sig=replace(msg, "\d+", "N")
| stats count latest(_time) as last_seen by host component msg_sig
| convert ctime(last_seen)
